### Tailwind-Testing

- Run the project's visual-regression tests when a theme token changes: every utility generated from it changes with it.
- Fail the lint or test step on a class name built at runtime, with a Tailwind-aware lint rule or a source search, whichever the project uses; the build drops such a class without reporting it.
<!-- Project-specific / Tailwind-Testing -->

### Tailwind-Common Mistakes

- Runtime-built class: a class name built by interpolation or concatenation (`` `bg-${color}-600` ``) => map each variant to its complete class list.
- Copy-pasted class list: the same long class list repeated across components => extract it into one component or template partial.
- `@apply` everywhere: a stylesheet made mostly of `@apply` rules, rebuilding the component classes utilities replace => style the markup with utilities, and extract components.
- Arbitrary token: arbitrary values (`top-[13px]`, `text-[#3457d5]`) standing in for a theme token => add the token to the theme and use its utility.
- Conflicting utilities: two utilities setting the same CSS property on one element, or caller classes appended without merging => pick one with a conditional, or merge with the project's class-merging utility.
<!-- Project-specific / Tailwind-Common Mistakes -->
